  "content": "Heavy rain risk eases in Kathmandu Valley, shifts to Koshi Province\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 5, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 5\nMeteorologists have said that rainfall remains likely due to the moisture-laden monsoon winds from the Bay of Bengal.\nHowever, the weather system capable of triggering heavy downpours has weakened in the Kathmandu Valley and has now shifted towards Koshi Province. According to the Department of Hydrology and Meteorology, the threat of heavy rain in Kathmandu has subsided.\n“The system has already weakened in Bagmati Province, including Kathmandu Valley, and the risk of heavy rainfall is over,” said senior meteorologist Min Kumar Aryal in an interview with Onlinekhabar.\nWhile rain clouds are still present in Madhesh Province, the possibility of downpours similar to yesterday is lower, he added.\nAt present, the rainfall system is concentrated in Koshi Province, leading to heavy to very heavy rainfall in several areas from Panchthar, Ilam, and Jhapa to the Terai plains of Chatara. Isolated heavy rainfall is still expected in parts of Ilam and the Terai belt of Koshi Province today, but this too is likely to weaken by afternoon, Aryal said.\nIn the past 24 hours, many areas of Koshi, Madhesh, and Bagmati provinces have experienced heavy to extremely heavy rainfall. The highest precipitation was recorded at Maheshpur station in Rautahat, measuring 351 millimeters.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nCOVID-19 Nepal\nKP Sharma Oli\nNepal covid-19\nCPN-UML\nNepali Congress\nNepal\nNepalelection\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nLong-distance travel from Kathmandu remains suspended, tickets to be refunded\n2 days ago\nTravel in and out of Kathmandu Valley halted for 3 days\n3 days ago\nNearly 200 thousand people leave Kathmandu Valley in five days\n2 weeks ago\nKathmandu in ruins (Photos)\n4 weeks ago\nOf Gods and Goddesses: Kathmandu readies for the spectacle of Indra Jatra\n1 month ago\nTwo youths killed in bus-scooter collision in Kathmandu\n1 month ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nManaslu climbing in autumn starts on encouraging note; Nima Chhiring sets new record\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nClay and culture: The making of Durga idols\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n2 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n2 months ago\nAlso Read\nDisaster\nNighttime vehicle movement banned indefinitely on Hetauda–Kathmandu short route\n19 hours ago\nDisaster\nHundreds stranded on Everest’s eastern side after heavy snowfall\n22 hours ago\nDisaster\nFloods and landslides obstruct roads at 19 locations in Koshi and Bagmati Provinces\n1 day ago\nDisaster\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\n2 days ago\nDisaster\nHeavy rain risk eases in Kathmandu Valley, shifts to Koshi Province\n2 days ago",
